1
00:00:00,161 --> 00:00:02,955
Here's a crane, seen from above, turning at

2
00:00:02,975 --> 00:00:03,759
a steady rate.

3
00:00:04,503 --> 00:00:06,349
The tip of its jib goes round and

4
00:00:06,431 --> 00:00:09,181
round a circle, and its speed never changes.

5
00:00:10,005 --> 00:00:12,395
Each of these arrows shows the tip's velocity

6
00:00:12,536 --> 00:00:14,243
at one moment, and they're all the same

7
00:00:14,284 --> 00:00:14,504
length.

8
00:00:15,269 --> 00:00:15,933
So here's a question.

9
00:00:16,639 --> 00:00:18,727
Is the tip of the jib accelerating?

10
00:00:19,356 --> 00:00:19,923
Make a prediction.

11
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,739
Speed only tells you how fast something's going.

12
00:00:27,302 --> 00:00:30,500
Velocity tells you how fast, and which way.

13
00:00:31,206 --> 00:00:33,043
Look at the four arrows copied side by

14
00:00:33,104 --> 00:00:33,366
side.

15
00:00:33,808 --> 00:00:35,491
They're the same length, so the speed is

16
00:00:35,531 --> 00:00:38,176
the same, but they point four different ways,

17
00:00:38,497 --> 00:00:40,440
so the velocity is different each time.

18
00:00:41,365 --> 00:00:44,177
Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity,

19
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:45,061
not of speed.

20
00:00:45,745 --> 00:00:48,574
So yes, the tip is accelerating, the whole

21
00:00:48,615 --> 00:00:49,075
way round.

22
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:51,867
Moving in a circle at a constant speed

23
00:00:51,908 --> 00:00:54,919
like this is called uniform circular motion.

24
00:00:55,776 --> 00:00:57,582
So which way is the velocity changing?

25
00:00:58,226 --> 00:00:59,800
Take two moments a little apart.

26
00:01:00,386 --> 00:01:02,297
Copy their velocity arrows so they start from

27
00:01:02,338 --> 00:01:02,921
the same point.

28
00:01:03,666 --> 00:01:06,274
The change in velocity, delta v, is the

29
00:01:06,435 --> 00:01:07,939
arrow that takes you from the tip of

30
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,805
the first to the tip of the second.

31
00:01:10,629 --> 00:01:12,715
Now bring the two moments closer and closer

32
00:01:12,756 --> 00:01:13,137
together.

33
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,891
The change ends up pointing straight at the

34
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:16,917
centre of the circle.

35
00:01:17,541 --> 00:01:19,828
So the acceleration points towards the centre too.

36
00:01:20,591 --> 00:01:24,557
It's called centripetal acceleration, which means centre-seeking, and

37
00:01:24,598 --> 00:01:26,761
it's always at right angles to the velocity.

38
00:01:27,976 --> 00:01:29,642
To put numbers on this, we need a

39
00:01:29,724 --> 00:01:31,933
few ways to describe circular motion.

40
00:01:32,738 --> 00:01:34,667
Here's a car going round a circular track

41
00:01:34,789 --> 00:01:36,074
of radius fifty metres.

42
00:01:36,618 --> 00:01:38,674
It takes twelve seconds to do one lap.

43
00:01:39,239 --> 00:01:42,066
That's the period, capital T, the time for

44
00:01:42,208 --> 00:01:43,350
one complete revolution.

45
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:44,875
The frequency, f,

46
00:01:45,718 --> 00:01:48,246
is the number of revolutions each second, so

47
00:01:48,528 --> 00:01:49,590
f equals one over T.

48
00:01:50,895 --> 00:01:53,063
We can also describe how fast it turns.

49
00:01:53,767 --> 00:01:56,033
An angle in radians is the arc length

50
00:01:56,154 --> 00:01:57,337
divided by the radius,

51
00:01:57,859 --> 00:02:00,487
so one full lap is two pi radians.

52
00:02:01,491 --> 00:02:05,207
Angular velocity, omega, is the angle turned divided

53
00:02:05,268 --> 00:02:06,252
by the time taken.

54
00:02:06,756 --> 00:02:08,789
For one lap, that's two pi over T.

55
00:02:09,689 --> 00:02:11,035
Let's find the car's speed.

56
00:02:11,659 --> 00:02:14,476
In one period it travels one circumference, two

57
00:02:14,517 --> 00:02:15,059
pi r.

58
00:02:15,622 --> 00:02:18,246
So v equals two pi r over T,

59
00:02:18,829 --> 00:02:21,513
which is two pi times fifty, over twelve.

60
00:02:22,096 --> 00:02:24,754
That's about twenty-six point two metres per second.

61
00:02:25,459 --> 00:02:28,388
Omega is two pi over twelve, about zero

62
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:30,857
point five two four radians per second.

63
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,388
And the frequency is one over twelve,

64
00:02:33,911 --> 00:02:36,462
about zero point zero eight three three hertz.

65
00:02:37,146 --> 00:02:37,627
As a check,

66
00:02:38,131 --> 00:02:39,939
f times T should equal one,

67
00:02:40,583 --> 00:02:40,964
and it does.

68
00:02:41,555 --> 00:02:44,062
Put those together and you get v equals

69
00:02:44,404 --> 00:02:45,145
omega r,

70
00:02:45,728 --> 00:02:48,055
because two pi over T is just omega.

71
00:02:49,079 --> 00:02:50,657
This explains something about the crane.

72
00:02:51,481 --> 00:02:53,422
Every point on the jib turns through the

73
00:02:53,463 --> 00:02:56,024
same angle in the same time, so every

74
00:02:56,065 --> 00:02:57,485
point has the same omega.

75
00:02:58,326 --> 00:03:00,169
But a point twice as far out goes

76
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:01,733
round a circle twice as big,

77
00:03:02,375 --> 00:03:04,017
so it moves twice as fast.

78
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:08,069
When omega is fixed, speed grows in proportion

79
00:03:08,231 --> 00:03:08,792
to the radius.

80
00:03:09,536 --> 00:03:12,334
Now, how big is the centripetal acceleration?

81
00:03:13,059 --> 00:03:14,084
Here's a neat way to see it.

82
00:03:14,936 --> 00:03:15,544
Back to the car.

83
00:03:16,188 --> 00:03:18,112
Take its velocity arrows from all the way

84
00:03:18,193 --> 00:03:20,137
round and start them from one point.

85
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,524
As the car goes once round the track,

86
00:03:22,846 --> 00:03:24,912
the tip of its velocity arrow goes once

87
00:03:24,993 --> 00:03:27,360
round a circle too, a circle of radius

88
00:03:27,421 --> 00:03:27,641
v.

89
00:03:28,424 --> 00:03:30,927
The acceleration is how fast the velocity changes,

90
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:33,412
so it's the distance that tip travels, two

91
00:03:33,453 --> 00:03:35,635
pi v, divided by the period.

92
00:03:36,158 --> 00:03:38,172
And the period is two pi r over

93
00:03:38,233 --> 00:03:38,494
v.

94
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:41,407
Substitute that in, and the two pis cancel,

95
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:44,600
leaving a equals v squared over r.

96
00:03:45,383 --> 00:03:48,491
Using v equals omega r, that's also omega

97
00:03:48,512 --> 00:03:49,192
squared r.

98
00:03:49,802 --> 00:03:52,677
For the car, a equals twenty-six point two

99
00:03:52,798 --> 00:03:53,944
squared, over fifty.

100
00:03:54,527 --> 00:03:56,918
That's about thirteen point seven metres per second

101
00:03:56,938 --> 00:03:58,666
squared, towards the centre.

102
00:03:59,189 --> 00:04:01,283
That's bigger than the acceleration of a falling

103
00:04:01,343 --> 00:04:01,646
object.

104
00:04:02,472 --> 00:04:03,666
And notice the square.

105
00:04:04,433 --> 00:04:06,800
At the same radius, twice the speed means

106
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:08,404
four times the acceleration.

107
00:04:09,127 --> 00:04:11,355
At the same speed, twice the radius means

108
00:04:11,536 --> 00:04:12,519
half the acceleration.

109
00:04:13,209 --> 00:04:15,679
Newton's second law says the net force points

110
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,387
the same way as the acceleration.

111
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:20,751
So anything in uniform circular motion needs a

112
00:04:20,832 --> 00:04:23,833
net force pointing towards the centre, of size

113
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,274
m v squared over r.

114
00:04:26,017 --> 00:04:27,932
This is called the centripetal force.

115
00:04:28,417 --> 00:04:30,276
But it isn't a new kind of force.

116
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:32,485
It's just a name for a job that

117
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:33,709
real forces do,

118
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:36,861
the overall push or pull towards the centre.

119
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:40,696
Tension, friction, gravity or a normal force can

120
00:04:40,737 --> 00:04:42,765
do that job, on their own or together.

121
00:04:43,436 --> 00:04:45,204
A common idea is that things moving in

122
00:04:45,225 --> 00:04:46,913
a circle get flung outwards.

123
00:04:47,517 --> 00:04:49,701
Picture a steel ball on a smooth table,

124
00:04:50,063 --> 00:04:52,047
kept in a circle by a string tied

125
00:04:52,068 --> 00:04:52,548
to a peg.

126
00:04:53,414 --> 00:04:54,147
Now cut the string.

127
00:04:54,873 --> 00:04:56,915
With no net force, the ball keeps the

128
00:04:56,936 --> 00:04:59,179
velocity it had at that instant, and it

129
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,022
moves off in a straight line along the

130
00:05:01,064 --> 00:05:03,747
tangent, the line that just touches the circle.

131
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:06,279
It doesn't fly straight out from the centre.

132
00:05:06,905 --> 00:05:08,377
Nothing was ever pushing it outwards.

133
00:05:08,802 --> 00:05:10,570
The string was only ever pulling it in.

134
00:05:11,563 --> 00:05:13,255
Here's a quick way to remember why the

135
00:05:13,316 --> 00:05:14,122
square matters.

136
00:05:14,704 --> 00:05:16,969
Twice as fast, four times the pull.

137
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:19,793
That holds when the mass and the radius

138
00:05:19,893 --> 00:05:22,236
stay the same, because the force needed is

139
00:05:22,537 --> 00:05:24,259
m v squared over r.

140
00:05:27,164 --> 00:05:27,528
Your turn.

141
00:05:28,492 --> 00:05:30,994
A laboratory rotor has a radius of zero

142
00:05:31,034 --> 00:05:33,957
point three zero metres and completes four point

143
00:05:33,977 --> 00:05:35,338
zero revolutions per second.

144
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:38,846
Calculate the angular velocity of the rotor, the

145
00:05:38,906 --> 00:05:40,470
speed of a point on its rim,

146
00:05:41,092 --> 00:05:43,297
and the centripetal acceleration of that point.

147
00:05:44,084 --> 00:05:44,974
Pause here to answer.

148
00:05:55,775 --> 00:05:59,184
Four revolutions per second means omega is two

149
00:05:59,245 --> 00:06:02,514
pi times four point zero, about twenty-five point

150
00:06:02,635 --> 00:06:03,717
one radians per second.

151
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:07,601
The rim speed is omega r, twenty-five point

152
00:06:07,722 --> 00:06:10,583
one times zero point three zero, about seven

153
00:06:10,624 --> 00:06:11,924
point five metres per second.

154
00:06:12,645 --> 00:06:15,692
And a is v squared over r, about

155
00:06:15,773 --> 00:06:17,737
one hundred and ninety metres per second squared.

156
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:21,404
The classic slip is writing omega as four,

157
00:06:21,906 --> 00:06:24,571
but four is the frequency in hertz, not

158
00:06:24,612 --> 00:06:25,492
the angle per second.

159
00:06:27,043 --> 00:06:27,468
Last one.

160
00:06:28,312 --> 00:06:31,415
Two identical cars travel around the same circular

161
00:06:31,456 --> 00:06:32,897
track at constant speeds.

162
00:06:33,519 --> 00:06:35,735
Car B travels at twice the speed of

163
00:06:35,776 --> 00:06:36,300
car A.

164
00:06:36,883 --> 00:06:40,215
Compare their centripetal accelerations, and the net forces

165
00:06:40,276 --> 00:06:40,497
on them.

166
00:06:41,263 --> 00:06:42,136
Pause here to answer.

167
00:06:52,763 --> 00:06:54,638
Same track, so the same radius.

168
00:06:55,202 --> 00:06:58,691
Acceleration is v squared over r, so doubling

169
00:06:58,791 --> 00:07:01,398
v makes it two squared, four times as

170
00:07:01,438 --> 00:07:01,659
big.

171
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:04,045
The cars are identical, so they have the

172
00:07:04,085 --> 00:07:06,512
same mass, and the net force is four

173
00:07:06,552 --> 00:07:07,454
times as big too.

174
00:07:08,216 --> 00:07:10,638
The slip is saying twice, which forgets that

175
00:07:10,679 --> 00:07:11,600
the speed is squared.

176
00:07:13,187 --> 00:07:15,308
So a car going round a bend at

177
00:07:15,349 --> 00:07:18,752
a steady speed is accelerating towards the centre,

178
00:07:19,494 --> 00:07:21,515
and something has to provide a net force

179
00:07:21,556 --> 00:07:22,396
towards the centre.

180
00:07:23,079 --> 00:07:24,649
Here's a car on a flat roundabout.

181
00:07:25,212 --> 00:07:27,641
Its weight pulls down, and the road pushes

182
00:07:27,762 --> 00:07:27,841
up.

183
00:07:28,366 --> 00:07:30,943
So which real force can pull it inwards?

184
00:07:33,695 --> 00:07:34,517
Here are the key notes.

185
00:07:35,041 --> 00:07:36,588
Pause the video if you need more time

186
00:07:36,629 --> 00:07:37,050
to copy them.
